From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:50:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: first run defaults to Fog Of War and no shadows

Two settings that cost software OpenGL a lot, now off in a new config
(an existing config keeps its values; both are in Options > Graphics):

- Fog "Mist" enables GL fog, which swrast applies to every pixel drawn
  (_swrast_fog_rgba_span, 8-11% of the frame). "Fog Of War" doesn't:
  25 -> 28 fps on the profiling host.
- Shadows are stencil volumes drawn for every object: 28 -> 30 fps with
  a handful of units, more in a big battle. Alt+S turns them on.
---
 src/configuration.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/configuration.c b/src/configuration.c
index ea25eb0..123b95c 100644
--- a/src/configuration.c
+++ b/src/configuration.c
@@ -208,8 +208,15 @@ BOOL loadConfig(void)
 	}
 	else
 	{
+		// shadows are an extra stencil pass per object: too much for
+		// software OpenGL (Alt+S or Options turn them on)
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+		setDrawShadows(false);
+		setWarzoneKeyNumeric("shadows", false);
+#else
 		setDrawShadows(true);
 		setWarzoneKeyNumeric("shadows", true);
+#endif
 	}
 
 	// //////////////////////////
@@ -420,8 +427,15 @@ BOOL loadConfig(void)
 	}
 	else
 	{
+		// "Mist" is OpenGL fog on every pixel drawn; software OpenGL does
+		// it per pixel, so RISC OS defaults to "Fog Of War"
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+		war_SetFog(false);
+		setWarzoneKeyNumeric("visfog", 1);
+#else
 		war_SetFog(true);
 		setWarzoneKeyNumeric("visfog", 0);
+#endif
 	}
 
 	// //////////////////////////
